I’ve settled the rework shape: socket-service failures will be mapped at the readiness boundary as lane-fatal; all public operations will run one shared failure-disposition path; cleanup will keep channel ownership until `free` succeeds; and teardown will be represented by one shared task that joins all adapter-owned tasks before returning. I’m also replacing unbounded drain arrays with single shared cleanup/drain ownership and explicit operation caps.
