codex
The new socket-failure test exposed a real libssh2 teardown corner: if the socket fails mid-packet, libssh2 retains the exact nonblocking send operation and `session_free` cannot advance through a different packet. I’m fixing that without faking operation success: after reporting the lane-fatal error, teardown enters a local abort-drain mode that consumes only libssh2’s retained callback bytes, never writes them to the network, and then runs the normal destructors so custom allocations return to baseline.
apply patch
