@@ -5,6 +5,13 @@
 
 ## 2026-08-10
 
+### 1943 — libssh2 adapter closes review round 5 fatal teardown and ownership gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- ROOT CAUSE: Fatal socket failures were mapped inconsistently and could leave an apparently usable transport; automatic keepalive used its reply deadline while waiting behind KEX; teardown queues and task snapshots could grow or report optimistic zeros; and one-shot channel cleanup could discard a live libssh2 pointer after `EAGAIN`.
+- REWORK: One privacy-safe failure path now tears down every lane-fatal socket error. Automatic keepalive defers behind an active rekey and starts a fresh reply deadline after gate admission. Session/channel admission is capped, shared drains and teardown use single-flight tasks, and teardown cancels and joins all owned work before clearing handles. Channel close/free remains tracked until libssh2 confirms disposal; cleanup failure retains ownership for session teardown.
+- NONBLOCKING CLEANUP: A terminal socket enters an abort-drain mode that feeds EOF to receives and consumes only libssh2's already-retained outbound bytes. This lets the engine complete its nonblocking destructors without network I/O or fabricated operation success. Session destruction is bounded; failure remains explicit and keeps ownership visible rather than claiming a closed baseline.
+- CONFORMANCE: Deterministic regressions cover socket failure during open/read/write/keepalive, keepalive delayed beyond its ordinary reply timeout by KEX, exec-start rejection plus repeated free `EAGAIN`, concurrent close pressure, and the 64-operation channel cap. Deferred receive credit, RFC open reasons, exact exec-exit metadata, and deep rekey/keepalive observability remain explicit unsupported states owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`.
+- VERIFICATION: `swift test --filter LibSSH2` passes 35 tests/3 suites; `make validate-core` passes 369 tests/31 suites plus build and boundary checks; `make validate-libssh2`, source tamper gates, and the dual-architecture extension-safe macOS provider/harness matrix exit 0. Strict recursive Swift format and diff checks pass. Logs use task-scoped `*-06.log` or later names under `.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/`.
+
 ### 1858 — libssh2 adapter closes review round 4 cancellation and cleanup gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
 - ROOT CAUSE: Long-lived reads reused the write-credit deadline; the authentication timeout raced a waiter that still joined an independently owned signer; rekey and keepalive deadlines began only after the shared session gate; and canceled upload cleanup inherited task cancellation, causing its cleanup progress handler to close the shared TCP bridge.
 - REWORK: Reads now wait without an implicit idle deadline while retaining operation-scoped cancellation. Socket and signer completion waiters let callers detach promptly, while teardown cancels and joins owned work. Rekey uses the earlier of the caller-visible explicit deadline and `SSHRekeyPolicy.timeout` before gate admission; one keepalive may queue behind KEX. EOF takes the per-channel write gate after accepted writes, and uncertain EOF/exec/upload failures run bounded uncancelled channel reset while siblings survive.
