+# TASK-260715-1ozsb6 developer outcome
+
+Date: 2026-08-10
+Role: developer
+Disposition: ready for review
+
+## Outcome
+
+The pinned libssh2/OpenSSL adapter is integrated behind the neutral SSH transport boundary for the macOS provider and harness. No libssh2 type crosses the shared contract. The adapter uses nonblocking readiness plus `LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN`, bounded gates and buffers, deterministic deadlines/cancellation, raw pre-authentication host-key evidence, approved external public-key signing, direct-tcpip, bidirectional exec, stdin upload, client/server rekey handling, keepalive, available metrics, allocator tracking, and privacy-safe typed errors.
+
+Review round 5 findings are closed:
+
+- Socket failures during channel open, read, write, and manual keepalive all produce lane-scoped `connectionLost`, enter one shared teardown, and return owned resources to baseline.
+- Automatic keepalive may wait behind a longer active KEX; its reply deadline begins after admission, and later scheduled keepalives continue.
+- Session and channel operation admission is capped at 64. Drain and teardown coordination is single-flight, and resource snapshots await actual task joins.
+- Exec-start rejection and channel close/free retain their live libssh2 pointer across `EAGAIN`; records are removed only after confirmed disposal. Terminal sockets use bounded abort-drain solely to complete libssh2's retained nonblocking state without further network I/O or fabricated success.
+- The loopback fixture now has bounded process shutdown, preventing a dead OpenSSH child from hanging a test executor.
+
+The four M3-deferred semantics remain explicit `unsupported` reports with owner `TASK-260728-3cveay`: consumer-driven receive credit, RFC channel-open reason taxonomy, exact exec-exit metadata, and deep rekey/keepalive observability. No value is inferred or silently substituted.
+
+## Validation evidence
+
+All commands below completed with exit code 0:
+
+- `swift test --filter LibSSH2AdapterIntegrationTests`: 17 tests / 1 suite (`.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/swift-test-integration-11.log`).
+- `swift test --filter LibSSH2`: 35 tests / 3 suites (`.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/swift-test-libssh2-07.log`).
+- `make validate-core`: 369 tests / 31 suites, build and boundary checks green (`.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/make-validate-core-06.log`). This closes the prior review's full-gate failure.
+- `make validate-libssh2` (`.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/make-validate-libssh2-06.log`). Its `count=-43` diagnostic is the intentional injected failure exercised before successful rekey recovery.
+- `make test-libssh2-source-gates` (`.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/make-test-libssh2-source-gates-06.log`).
+- `make native-apple-matrix`: macOS provider and harness, arm64 and x86_64 production builds, application-extension mode, pinned static libssh2/OpenSSL linkage (`.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/make-native-apple-matrix-06.log`).
+- `swift format lint --recursive --strict Package.swift Sources Tests` and `git diff --check`, rerun after final documentation edits, exit 0.
+- `task-board validate` exits 0 while reporting the pre-existing `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` for `STORY-260715-lkshfz` (`to-dev` versus this child in `development`). No parent/dependency status or unsupported gate was bypassed.
+
+## Architecture and lifecycle notes
+
+`ReluxTunnelLibSSH2Adapter` is linked only into the macOS provider and harness graphs; Core, the shared native adapter, and iOS products remain independent. Teardown closes the socket, drains socket/signature work, cancels and joins automatic rekey/keepalive tasks, disposes channels, then frees the session. A failed bounded destructor remains visible as failed ownership instead of being reported as closed. Repeated connect/cancel and concurrent close regressions reconcile sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, custom allocations, and buffered bytes to zero.
